# Detail views: always show important fields

On entity detail / overview screens, **do not hide important profile fields** when the value is missing.

Show the label and an empty placeholder (`emptyValue` / `—`) instead of omitting the row or the whole panel.

## Important fields (examples)

* Contact: email, phone
* Links: website, Facebook, Google Maps, founded year
* Address (current and former): province, ward/district, address line
* Description / short intro
* Sports / categories tied to the entity

## Allowed to omit

* Entire **optional chrome** that is not a field (e.g. map widget when there are no coordinates)
* Secondary marketing / list empty-states that are not labeled profile fields
* `public_id` and any “Public ID” label. It is an internal token. Business codes (court code, branch code) stay visible.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — hide when empty
{website ? <ProfileRow label="Website" value={website} /> : null}
{description ? <Panel>...</Panel> : null}

// ✅ GOOD — always show, placeholder when empty
<ProfileRow label="Website" value={website || empty} />
<Panel>{description ? <RichTextView html={description} /> : empty}</Panel>
```

## Bilingual fields resolve to the active locale

Do not render a `*_en` field, or a label that says “(EN)”, on a read surface.

A field stored as `_vi` and `_en` shows **one** value: the copy for the current locale, then the other locale, then the empty placeholder. The same resolution applies to the page title when the record has localized names.

Forms may still submit both columns. Only the read surface collapses them.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — two language rows
<ProfileRow label={t("fieldNameVi")} value={court.name_vi} />
<ProfileRow label={t("fieldNameEn")} value={court.name_en} />

// ✅ GOOD — locale, then the other locale, then the placeholder
const name = locale.startsWith("vi")
  ? court.name_vi?.trim() || court.name_en?.trim()
  : court.name_en?.trim() || court.name_vi?.trim();
<ProfileRow label={t("fieldName")} value={name || empty} />
```

## Relation fields use `EntityRelationLink`

A profile value that navigates to another Bokdy entity is `EntityRelationLink` (`apps/admin-web/components/entity/relation-link.tsx`). Do not style that link with `text-sky-*` or `dark:text-sky-*`.

When the related record is loaded, the link shows its name. When it is not loaded, show the id or the empty placeholder as plain text.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — one-off sky classes
<Link href={`/branches/${branch.id}`} className="text-sky-700 font-medium dark:text-sky-300">
  {branch.name}
</Link>

// ✅ GOOD
<EntityRelationLink href={`/branches/${branch.id}`}>{branch.name}</EntityRelationLink>
```
